[{:db/id 17592186171930 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c18b42a5-90d9-54a8-87df-2489d5f7b5e0" "question-7927d3cc-3f03-52c6-bf05-98c129843c5c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186171931 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fbf3d356-bb6f-5d45-9a65-7f6a6ff861ab" "question-65f2c34a-43ea-5ba9-8212-652326193c1e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186409537 :question/problem "Consider the following false statement.\n\n$9n-4$ is even for any $n\\in Z$\n\nA counterexample for this statement would be an integer {{field-1}} such that {{field-2}} is {{field-3}}." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172425 :question/problem "Consider the following false statement.\n\n${n}^{2}-6n+8\\ge 0$ for any $n\\in N.$\n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be an integer $n$ such that \n\n$$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-c18b42a5-90d9-54a8-87df-2489d5f7b5e0" :question/id #uuid "c18b42a5-90d9-54a8-87df-2489d5f7b5e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-221707" :question/problem "Disprove the following statement:\n\n$6∣{n}^{2}+2$ for any $n\\in Z.$\n\nTo {{field-1}} a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a {{field-2}}. \nIn other words, we need to show that {{field-3}}\n\n$$\n6{{field-4}}{n}^{2}+2.\n$$\n\nNotice that by substituting $n=$ {{field-5}} into the expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}+2 & =({{field-6}})^{2}+2 \\\\  & ={{field-7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is {{field-8}} by $6.$ \n\nSo, $n=$ {{field-9}} is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." :question/worked-solution "Our statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀n\\in Z,\\,6∣{n}^{2}+2.\n$$\n\nWe want to disprove this statement. In other words, we must show that its negation is true:\n\n$$\n¬(∀n\\in Z,\\,6∣{n}^{2}+2)\\,≡\\,∃n\\in Z,\\,6∤{n}^{2}+2\n$$\n\nSo, we begin as follows:\n\nTo disprove a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a counterexample. In other words, we need to show that there exists an integer $n$ such that \n\n$$\n6∤{n}^{2}+2.\n$$\n\nFinding a counterexample is sometimes a nontrivial task, but we only need one. In this case, substituting $n=0$ suffices:\n\nNotice that by substituting $n=0$ into the expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}+2 & =(0)^{2}+2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $6.$ \n\nFinally, we state our conclusion:\n\nSo, $n=0$ is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-45cf8aa7-7fd6-5ad7-af3e-d4fdebd34db5" "answer-field-9e4be0b5-040a-5119-8ff6-b47550c1d235" "answer-field-ad4e1c57-a86f-5d23-8245-4f4517e84720" "answer-field-d5e3f846-8b1d-584b-b03b-c049b60f2fd7" "answer-field-d39292c6-4779-524c-b09b-0a8df489f189" "answer-field-e93254f9-d285-52fc-8b88-774e0e8838df" "answer-field-9155436b-9793-5efe-99ab-ae1e516a435f" "answer-field-1cfb41f4-65b1-590a-a841-7a4aea9b39fd" "answer-field-4e20d187-477e-53e6-9754-6079826aa601"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-45cf8aa7-7fd6-5ad7-af3e-d4fdebd34db5" :answer-field/id #uuid "45cf8aa7-7fd6-5ad7-af3e-d4fdebd34db5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-5b6b7348-a1ae-5619-8f5e-48488f993fe4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5b6b7348-a1ae-5619-8f5e-48488f993fe4" "answer-8ab31b7b-35eb-5066-8e7c-7850efee8543"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5b6b7348-a1ae-5619-8f5e-48488f993fe4" :answer/id #uuid "5b6b7348-a1ae-5619-8f5e-48488f993fe4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "disprove" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ab31b7b-35eb-5066-8e7c-7850efee8543" :answer/id #uuid "8ab31b7b-35eb-5066-8e7c-7850efee8543" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "prove" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9e4be0b5-040a-5119-8ff6-b47550c1d235" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e4be0b5-040a-5119-8ff6-b475