d #uuid "1cfb41f4-65b1-590a-a841-7a4aea9b39fd" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-14636d7c-818e-5692-8f6f-3fb7e7a22eb1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2ea91716-687e-5920-b491-b99a0e733edf" "answer-14636d7c-818e-5692-8f6f-3fb7e7a22eb1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2ea91716-687e-5920-b491-b99a0e733edf" :answer/id #uuid "2ea91716-687e-5920-b491-b99a0e733edf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "divisible" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14636d7c-818e-5692-8f6f-3fb7e7a22eb1" :answer/id #uuid "14636d7c-818e-5692-8f6f-3fb7e7a22eb1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "not divisible" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4e20d187-477e-53e6-9754-6079826aa601" :answer-field/id #uuid "4e20d187-477e-53e6-9754-6079826aa601" :answer-field/key "field-9" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-97ac1294-8d1b-58b8-804e-7909d15e0fd1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-97ac1294-8d1b-58b8-804e-7909d15e0fd1" "answer-20ef4ace-1bde-5f25-89d2-14c5b107dbf7" "answer-6054268f-4fcf-5a5f-8727-4c6e93ec25df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97ac1294-8d1b-58b8-804e-7909d15e0fd1" :answer/id #uuid "97ac1294-8d1b-58b8-804e-7909d15e0fd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20ef4ace-1bde-5f25-89d2-14c5b107dbf7" :answer/id #uuid "20ef4ace-1bde-5f25-89d2-14c5b107dbf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6054268f-4fcf-5a5f-8727-4c6e93ec25df" :answer/id #uuid "6054268f-4fcf-5a5f-8727-4c6e93ec25df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7927d3cc-3f03-52c6-bf05-98c129843c5c" :question/id #uuid "7927d3cc-3f03-52c6-bf05-98c129843c5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-221701" :question/problem "Disprove the following statement:\n\n$5n+2$ is odd for any $n\\in Z.$\n\nTo {{field-1}} a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a {{field-2}}. \nIn other words, we need to show that {{field-3}} \n$5n+2$ is {{field-4}}.\n\nNotice that by substituting $n=$ {{field-5}} into the expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5n+2 & =5({{field-6}})+2 \\\\  & ={{field-7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is {{field-8}}. \n\nSo, $n=$ {{field-9}} is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." :question/worked-solution "Our statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀n\\in Z,\\,5n+2\\text{ is odd}.\n$$\n\nWe want to disprove this statement. In other words, we must show that its negation is true:\n\n$$\n¬(∀n\\in Z,\\,5n+2\\text{ is odd})\\,≡\\,∃n\\in Z,\\,5n+2\\text{ is even}\n$$\n\nSo, we begin as follows:\n\nTo disprove a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a counterexample. In other words, we need to show that there exists an integer $n$ such that $5n+2$ is even.\n\nFinding a counterexample is sometimes a nontrivial task, but we only need one. In this case, substituting $n=0$ suffices:\n\nNotice that by substituting $n=0$ into the expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5n+2 & =5(0)+2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is even. \n\nFinally, we state our conclusion:\n\nSo, $n=0$ is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-03fc8aaa-3047-551e-96b6-c20a42fc7aa2" "answer-field-cda2e076-6739-5467-a75b-c1a4130c6fd9" "answer-field-14c66781-f781-529d-83e4-493849b79650" "answer-field-f28e58e2-4175-5117-9b69-4f36deb6b8ca" "answer-field-92f50238-4639-5e3c-9818-cb8a92d5a14f" "answer-field-5e545396-dfe8-5732-ade5-cc97b9e92212" "answer-field-2cf51a18-e2fb-5b4a-92e0-f4eea96cfd57" "answer-field-d5fedbdb-836a-5ee4-a0da-26b933ce8c11" "answer-field-5ac2d55c-ad24-5f8a-aebe-82884d04e272"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-03fc8aaa-3047-551e-96b6-c20a42fc7aa2" :answer-field/id #uuid "03fc8aaa-3047-55