atement. In other words, we must show that its negation is true:\n\n$$\n¬(∀x\\in R,\\,{x}^{2}+5x+6\\ge 0)\\,≡\\,∃x\\in R,\\,{x}^{2}+5x+6<0\n$$\n\nSo, we begin as follows:\n\nTo disprove a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a counterexample. In other words, we need to show that there exists a real number $x$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+5x+6<0.\n$$\n\nFinding a counterexample is sometimes a nontrivial task, but we only need one. In this case, substituting $x=-2.5$ suffices:\n\nBy substituting $x=-2.5$ into the expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+5x+6 & =(-2.5)^{2}+5(-2.5)+6 \\\\  & =-0.25 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we state our conclusion:\n\nSo, $x=-2.5$ is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d6f22d6f-482f-5f8a-bf60-63d26ce12b81" "answer-field-99dfee88-dfe0-58a1-8612-fb8206ae22c4" "answer-field-698ed6c3-30d5-53da-9f5f-bf1e53b172f0" "answer-field-2aa039a6-1aaa-582c-a79c-580873fe5a74" "answer-field-5837de9f-0422-5e54-8c02-c83c737b7086" "answer-field-6c8ce777-e389-5e60-94b0-ffa944e9e9a0" "answer-field-14715ea5-6dfa-5a80-a5ef-10c41c497286" "answer-field-dab95909-e45b-53f1-bf4f-61cf81c795fb" "answer-field-2c0038a5-cebf-596b-8b63-34cd20469b7f" "answer-field-58b4d742-a574-55eb-95cd-79c90c60f20e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d6f22d6f-482f-5f8a-bf60-63d26ce12b81" :answer-field/id #uuid "d6f22d6f-482f-5f8a-bf60-63d26ce12b81" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-a1056cdb-e9cc-5a85-bfb3-0a2f5c17636a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a1056cdb-e9cc-5a85-bfb3-0a2f5c17636a" "answer-80293b1d-10bc-5497-b2e7-2fc622ce4bf3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1056cdb-e9cc-5a85-bfb3-0a2f5c17636a" :answer/id #uuid "a1056cdb-e9cc-5a85-bfb3-0a2f5c17636a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "disprove" :db/ensure [:answer/valid