 In other words, we must show that its negation is true:\n\n$$\n¬(∀n\\in N,\\,11n-{n}^{2}-28\\le 0)\\,≡\\,∃n\\in N,\\,11n-{n}^{2}-28>0\n$$\n\nSo, we begin as follows:\n\nTo disprove a universal statement, it's sufficient to find a counterexample. In other words, we need to show that there exists a natural number $n$ such that \n\n$$\n11n-{n}^{2}-28>0.\n$$\n\nFinding a counterexample is sometimes a nontrivial task, but we only need one. In this case, substituting $n=5$ suffices:\n\nBy substituting $n=5$ into the expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11n-{n}^{2}-28 & =11(5)-(5)^{2}-28 \\\\  & =2 \\\\  & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we state our conclusion:\n\nSo, $n=5$ is our counterexample. Therefore, the given statement is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8321e4fb-3390-5aef-a36f-82b7c2432ac7" "answer-field-dfca6545-c8c1-5004-8749-9df5ea279860" "answer-field-17c303ec-a913-565c-bdd7-25ed8399ba26" "answer-field-3b240b6b-5892-5007-9e33-589b54f48898" "answer-field-c95ff6e3-a3ea-50db-b9dd-0b9b04c365dc" "answer-field-61d6734d-2f58-5dd6-a85d-d9027af5026f" "answer-field-2f6e2ea7-ff0c-5867-aa7e-3326715381aa" "answer-field-f6bb26c4-97c0-5cb5-94f1-cbe41ac86d89" "answer-field-143d5a65-72d1-5d83-805d-3d4e7580a2f4" "answer-field-117a9f26-8c0e-5cf2-be80-8bbf61fa76c3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8321e4fb-3390-5aef-a36f-82b7c2432ac7" :answer-field/id #uuid "8321e4fb-3390-5aef-a36f-82b7c2432ac7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-004ce3ba-4979-5ef3-9750-384e369ab278" :answer-field/choices ["answer-004ce3ba-4979-5ef3-9750-384e369ab278" "answer-8f750b2a-7381-59c3-b43b-b1a1589dce57"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-004ce3ba-4979-5ef3-9750-384e369ab278" :answer/id #uuid "004ce3ba-4979-5ef3-9750-384e369ab278" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "disprove" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 